## Introduction

This TypeScript library provides a ticket-sorting functionality that allows you to sort ticket details based on their priority.

## Installation

To install this library, run the following command:
```bash
pnpm install
```

## Usage

In this example, we assume that there are two tickets, both with the same ID, `ticketId`. This example uses a simple ticket-sorting logic, where the tickets are sorted in ascending order based on their priority.

### Ticket-Sorter.ts

```typescript
import { sortTicket } from './ticketSorter';

function sortTicketsByPriority() {
  const tickets = [
    { id: 1, priority: 'High', title: 'High Priority Ticket' },
    { id: 2, priority: 'Medium', title: 'Medium Priority Ticket' },
    { id: 3, priority: 'Low', title: 'Low Priority Ticket' },
  ];

  const sortedTickets = tickets.sort((ticketA, ticketB) => {
    if (ticketA.priority === ticketB.priority) {
      return 0;
    }
    return ticketA.priority < ticketB.priority ? -1 : 1;
  });

  console.log(sortedTickets);
}
```

### ticketSorter.ts

